cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use radar.raman, please cite the article below."
type: software
title: "radar.raman: Raman Spectral Analysis Using Deep Learning for Artifact Removal"
abstract: >-
  R package that decomposes Raman spectra into baseline, cosmic rays, noise and
  Raman peaks using bundled pretrained standard and ensemble convolutional
  networks. Neural network inference, automatic differentiation, training,
  synthetic data generation, evaluation and spectral file conversion are
  implemented entirely in R, with readers and writers for the common
  spectroscopy formats. A port of the Python radar-raman package.
